{"step_index":1409,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T12:33:40Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. becaus yes the chatbot, evon though not human will have a hijman identty\n2. i  am connectd rfom 9 to worik on tit oncce live will be boutd to 127.0.0.1\n3. i will have my own isdetity, i plan on using this one for a few days\n4. `\n5. and the final chatbot will have no internet adccess either\n6. that has not been deterimined yet. right now i am estatic to have a root chatbot woking that can controll the system. it is gong to jmake developemntgg much faser ansd smoother\n7. next thing iws getting ht e vectoriazation working e2e and the memory oloop, cozo qdreahnt\n8. then teh ui\n9. then a demo\n10. sfirst tist all the cognative endpoingtws swee if all that funtionalty is 2orking\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Requests & Goals**:\n  1. Test all cognitive endpoints and verify end-to-end functionality across the memory loop (`Cozo` + `Qdrant`).\n  2. Implement/verify the Control Plane Chatbot architecture:\n     - The chatbot is the **sole root entity** on the system (`root:root`, UID 0).\n     - It has **zero direct execution rights** and **no internet access**; it operates strictly by **delegation** to bounded workers/subagents.\n     - Root-level operations proposed through the chatbot require **2-of-N cryptographic superadmin approvals** (derived from registered WireGuard public keys).\n     - For this root chatbot identity, the `Personal` section in the Svelte UI (`3tched.com`) must be hidden (only `Control Plane` and system sections visible).\n     - The chatbot has authority to edit the control-plane model and promote UI elements to the active catalog.\n     - User is connected from `10.0.0.9` to work on it; once live, the chatbot will be bound to `127.0.0.1` (Container 0). Do NOT drop the `10.0.0.9\n<truncated 6186 bytes>\nst `cognitive.memory_query` / `memory_recall` against Qdrant (`127.0.0.1:6334`) and Cozo\n   - Verify bi-temporal memory recall via `crates/op-cognitive/src/memory_store.rs` and `qdrant_shuttle.rs`.\n2. **Complete Slot B Activation**:\n   - Run `sudo ./activate-golden.sh` (or `sudo /usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch deploy` followed by `activate b`).\n   - Confirm `tched-router` stays up and clean overlay swap to Slot B succeeds.\n3. **Svelte UI (`3tched.com`) Updates**:\n   - Add \"New chat\" / \"Clear chat\" button in `src/svelte/Chat.svelte`.\n   - Hide `Personal` menu section when authenticated as the root Control Plane Chatbot.\n4. **Enforce 2-of-N Cryptographic Superadmin Policy**:\n   - Register superadmin public keys in capability policy.\n   - Enforce dual-signature gate for root delegated operations.\n5. **Run Full End-to-End Live Demo**:\n   - Ingest memory $\\rightarrow$ query via chatbot $\\rightarrow$ bi-temporal recall $\\rightarrow$ root delegation $\\rightarrow$ dynamic UI promotion.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Preserve User Connection**: Never disconnect or drop `10.0.0.9` while the operator is connected through it.\n- **Root Chatbot Invariant**: The chatbot is the single root entity on the system (`root:root`), but has zero direct execution and no internet access. All actions are delegated to bounded workers.\n- **Frontend Stack**: Strictly Svelte/SvelteKit + Vite + `@json-render/svelte`. Never introduce React or other renderers.\n- **Init Policy**: Runit only (`sudo sv <cmd> <service>`). Never use `systemctl`.\n- **Deployment**: Deployment is strictly Btrfs send/receive of prepared snapshots via `./activate-golden.sh`. Never hand-copy binaries onto live host targets.\n</summary>\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_full.jsonl`:\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl`","truncated_fields":["content"]}
